WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.140
Good morning. This is OmniView, episode SI-63 for May 28th, 2026.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.400
Balance news perspectives. We'll cover what happened, how different viewpoints frame it,

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:19.620
so you can decide for yourself. US core inflation rose to 3.3% in April while consumer spending

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:25.480
edge-tire, shaping expectations for interest-rate decisions that affect household costs nationwide.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:32.040
The Justice Department has opened a criminal probe into whether former columnist E. Jean Carroll

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:37.060
made false statements about funding for her civil lawsuit against President Trump.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.400
The inquiry focuses on the sources of money used in the earlier legal action.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.780
Details remain limited as the investigation is in early stages.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.020
Outlets tracking the case note that the probe examines financial disclosures tied to the lawsuit

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:59.260
rather than revisiting the underlying allegations. Groups supportive of the President view the move

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:04.900
as accountability for what they see as politically motivated litigation. Critics argue

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:11.080
it risks shilling future claims against public figures. Both sides agree the inquiry centers on

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:16.900
funding statements they differ on whether it represents standard legal scrutiny or targeted pressure.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.800
What evidence would clarify the funding claims under review?

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.480
Shifting now to developments in the Ukraine conflict, the EU's chief diplomat stated that Russia

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:34.260
faces mounting challenges on military, economic, and diplomatic fronts. The assessment comes amid

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:40.140
ongoing talks and battlefield developments. European officials framed the situation as one where

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:46.080
pressure on Russia is increasing across multiple fronts, potentially opening space for negotiations.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:53.300
Russian statements continue to emphasize resolve and reject external characterizations of weakness.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.540
Observers note that battlefield realities and sanctions effects form the factual basis.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:05.300
Interpretations differ on how quickly or decisively any shift will materialize.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.740
What measurable indicators support the EU assessment? Meanwhile, Iran has restored

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:18.600
internet access after an 88-day nationwide blockade. Connections to the outside world remain limited

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:24.840
by long-standing filters and controls. The blackout period produced documented economic and

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:31.160
social disruptions. Iranian authorities present the restoration as a return to normal operations

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:37.980
under existing rules. International observers and domestic users report that pre-blockade restrictions

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:44.460
continue to constrain information flow and business activity. Both accounts agree the blackout has

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:50.100
ended. They differ on the practical extent of restored connectivity, which sectors reported the

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:56.540
largest economic losses during the outage. The EU's top diplomat also called for Russian forces to

00:02:56.540 --> 00:03:03.200
withdraw from Moldova and Georgia as part of any Ukraine peace framework. The statement referenced

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:09.580
limits on Russian military size under a potential agreement. EU representatives tied the troop

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:15.640
withdrawals to broader regional security guarantees. Russian officials have historically rejected

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:22.080
external demands on forced posture in neighboring states. The factual disagreement centers on whether

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:28.400
such conditions form part of current talks or remain outside the immediate agenda. What legal or

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:33.340
treaty basis supports the withdrawal request? Turning to business developments,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:40.700
Actus reached at a $20.5 billion first close for its flagship energy fund. This amount represents

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:47.940
roughly 40% of the target. Fund managers present the result as evidence of sustained capital allocation

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:54.480
toward energy projects. Investors weigh returns potential against policy and technology risks in the

00:03:54.480 --> 00:04:00.760
space. The amount raised provides a concrete benchmark for current market appetite, which types

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:07.440
of energy projects does the fund target. In technology news, a report commissioned by environmental groups

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:14.500
calculated that data centers used 22% of Ireland's electricity last year. The centers added an

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:23.780
average of 360 euros to household bills between 2015 and 2023. The report authors link data center

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:30.620
growth to higher consumer costs and call for policy review. Industry representatives typically point

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:36.680
to economic benefits and job creation from the facilities. Both sides reference the same electricity

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:44.100
consumption data. They differ on net impact and appropriate regulatory response. How does Ireland's

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.700
data center share compare with other European countries? Now, to really understand this story,

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:56.480
there's something most coverage leaves out. The Federal Reserve's preferred core PCE measure strips

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:03.680
out volatile food and energy components to isolate underlying price trends. Those trends then

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:09.700
feed into economic models that project future inflation paths under different interest rate scenarios.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:16.180
Those projections combined with assessments of employment and financial conditions inform whether

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:22.220
officials lean toward holding rates steady, easing, or tightening. Next time you hear claims that

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:27.800
a single monthly reading forces a rate cut or hike, ask yourself which measure is being cited,

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:33.600
what other indicators are moving alongside it, and what historical episodes show similar readings

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:39.620
producing different outcomes. Tomorrow, watch for further updates on consumer spending patterns

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:44.620
and any shifts in Federal Reserve communications around the latest inflation figures.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:51.080
That wraps up today's omniview. Remember, the best informed people read more than one perspective.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:56.440
If this show helps you do that, share it with someone who values fair coverage. See you tomorrow.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:03.200
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice. Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
